# Copy to .env (gitignored). Never commit real values.
#
# kie.ai image/video generation. Two names are read because different tools in this
# repo grew up with different conventions; set BOTH to the same key:
#   KIE_AI_API_KEY  -> .claude/skills/nano-banana-images, excalidraw-visuals, scrollcraft (kie.mjs)
#   KIE_API_KEY     -> scripts/kie-assets.mjs (PR #168 connector); also accepted by the skills above
# Get the key from https://kie.ai -> account settings. Each generation spends credits.
KIE_AI_API_KEY=
KIE_API_KEY=
#
# For Claude Code on the web, add the same variable(s) to the environment's settings
# (Environment -> Environment variables) instead of a .env file, and allow api.kie.ai and
# kieai.redpandaai.co in that environment's network policy if generation should run there.
#
# Portal QA login for Digerati Experts test runs. Set the same names in the
# GitHub Actions repository secrets for the manual Portal production check.
# Local runs read the QA runner environment. The portal server ignores them.
# See docs/runbooks/PORTAL-QA-LOGIN.md. This does not create an account.
# Use a DE test company, never a client tenant. Never commit the values.
PORTAL_QA_EMAIL=
PORTAL_QA_PASSWORD=
